messages.content:
{
  "message": "Thanks, John. I found your account and the line ending in 2002 is Active. Because you’re abroad, I’ve just enabled international data roaming on our side for that line at no cost. You’ve used 8.7 GB out of 15 GB this cycle, so you still have data available—this likely isn’t a plan-limit issue. Next, please run the on‑device checks below in order and paste back the results. My reasoning is that MMS requires working cellular data with roaming, the correct MMSC/APN, and no Wi‑Fi/VPN/Wi‑Fi Calling conflicts. 1) Basic connectivity check: - Run check_status_bar and check_network_status. Confirm: Airplane Mode is OFF, you have at least some signal, network type is 3G/4G/5G, Mobile Data is ON, and Data Roaming is ON. - If Mobile Data is OFF, use toggle_data to turn it ON. - If Data Roaming is OFF, use toggle_roaming to turn it ON. 2) Eliminate Wi‑Fi/VPN/Wi‑Fi Calling conflicts: - Run check_wifi_status; if connected/on, use toggle_wifi to turn Wi‑Fi OFF. - Run check_vpn_status; if a VPN is active, use disconnect_vpn. - Run check_wifi_calling_status; if ON, use toggle_wifi_calling to turn it OFF. 3) Ensure modern network mode: - Run check_network_mode_preference. If it shows 2G/3G, set set_network_mode_preference to \"4g_5g_preferred\". 4) Verify APN/MMSC: - Run check_apn_settings. If MMSC is missing/blank or APN shows incorrect, use reset_apn_settings, then immediately run reboot_device to apply changes. 5) App capability and permissions: - Run check_app_permissions(app_name=\"messaging\"). If storage or sms are not granted, use grant_app_permission for both (\"storage\" and \"sms\"). 6) Test MMS: - Run can_send_mms. Then try sending a photo MMS to a known contact (or to your own number) and note any error shown. 7) If still failing: - Run run_speed_test and share the result. Please send me the outputs (or a quick summary) from each step above. Also let me know your phone type/model (iPhone or Android + model) so I can tailor any device-specific steps if needed. If anything is unclear, I can walk you through step by step."
}

