{
  "message": "Got it, John—I know that’s frustrating. Since roaming and data are now fixed, the next likely blocker is the MMS server info (MMSC) in your APN. Resetting APN forces the correct MMSC, and a reboot applies it. I can’t change your phone remotely, so please follow these steps on your device. Step 1 — Reset APN settings (this restores the correct MMSC): • If your device supports the “reset APN” action, please run: reset_apn_settings. • If you prefer manual steps: - iPhone: Settings > Cellular (or Mobile Data) > Cellular Data Network > scroll and tap Reset Settings (or Reset at the bottom). - Android: Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile Network > Access Point Names > menu (⋮) > Reset to default. Step 2 — Reboot your phone to apply APN changes: • Run: reboot_device. • Or manually power the phone OFF, wait 20 seconds, then power ON. Step 3 — Quick post-reboot check and test: • Make sure Airplane Mode is OFF. • Turn Mobile Data ON and Data Roaming ON. • Turn Wi‑Fi OFF just for the test. • Try sending a small photo MMS. Please go through Steps 1–3 now and tell me the result. As soon as you confirm you’ve completed the reset and reboot, we’ll immediately check Wi‑Fi Calling and turn it OFF if it’s enabled, then retest. I’m standing by."
}

